+| `internal/web/auth.go` | Routes `GET|POST /admin/login`; `loginForm` boundary parse (handlers never touch form/query again); POST CSRF-verified like every POST (`VerifyCSRF`, 403 on error); blank token (GET or POST) → 200 form; `tokenMatches` constant-time compare (see deviations); consume → `EnsureAdminUser` → `CreateSession(role "admin")` → `setSessionCookie` → `302 /admin`; replay → 403; store errors → logged 500. Minimal inline login page with exactly the frozen strings (`Admin login`, `Token`, `input name="token"`, `Sign in`), buffered render, `text/html; charset=utf-8`. T-205 replaces the markup via `pages/admin-login.html` — keep these strings byte-for-byte. |
